  ],
  "notes": "Composed of {加|か} (add/inflict) and {害|がい} (harm). Most commonly encountered in the compound {加害者|かがいしゃ} (perpetrator/offender), which pairs with {被害者|ひがいしゃ} (victim). The word frames harm from the perspective of the one causing it.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {加害者|かがいしゃ}: perpetrator, offender\n- {加害|かがい}{行為|こうい}: act of harm, harmful act\n- {加害|かがい}{側|がわ}: the perpetrating side\n- {加害|かがい}{責任|せきにん}: responsibility for harm caused\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {被害|ひがい}: damage suffered / victimization — the opposite perspective, receiving harm\n- {危害|きがい}: bodily harm / injury — focuses specifically on physical harm\n- {損害|そんがい}: damage / loss — focuses on material or financial damage\n\nNOTE ON HOMOPHONES:\nDo not confuse with {花街|かがい} (geisha district), which has the same reading.",
